  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Drier weather returns featuring cool overnights and \nwarm afternoons.\n\nClouds are gradually clearing this afternoon and will continue\nto do so into the overnight hours. Still seeing an area of \nstubborn overcast across the New River Valley being enhanced by\nthe upper low still progressing through the region. This key\nfeature will eventually move into the Atlantic and develop into\na strong low, which will eventually move up the Atlantic Coast.\nIn response to the strengthening low, flow turns more\nnorth/northwesterly tonight and any remaining cloud cover will\ndiminish giving way to clear skies by early Friday. \n\nCoolest temperatures since earlier this year are expected\ntonight with widespread lower 40s and even a few upper 30s\nacross the higher terrain...mid to upper 40s east of the\nmountains. Cooler temperatures will remain in place through the\nweekend, but will begin to moderate with return flow next week.\nNo rain expected for at least the next week.",
